<title>USA: U.S. Weekend Box Office Chart -- Dec 27-29.</title>
<headline>U.S. Weekend Box Office Chart -- Dec 27-29.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the December 27-29 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Michael		    $17,435,711	 $ 27,629,196</p>
<p>2. Jerry Maguire	    $14,024,111	 $ 60,351,092</p>
<p>3. 101 Dalmatians	   $11,384,660	 $104,111,652</p>
<p>4. Beavis and Butt-head</p>
<p>    Do America		$10,211,248	 $ 41,121,487</p>
<p>5. Scream			$9,075,667	 $ 21,253,204</p>
<p>6. One Fine Day		$8,027,257	 $ 19,435,044</p>
<p>7. The Preacher's Wife     $7,347,274	 $ 27,942,124</p>
<p>8. Mars Attacks!	     $5,075,963	 $ 25,846,508</p>
<p>9. My Fellow Americans     $4,166,630	 $ 10,170,986</p>
<p>10 The Evening Star	  $3,306,445	 $  5,272,449</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Michael&quot; was produced by now-defunct Turner Pictures, and released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc..  &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. &quot;101 Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;The Preacher's Wife&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Beavis and Butt-head Do America&quot; and &quot;The Evening Star&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney. &quot;One Fine Day&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..  &quot;Mars Attacks!&quot; and &quot;My Fellow Americans&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner.</p>
</text>
